---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import StatusPill from '../../components/StatusPill.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
---

<Layout
  title="Layers & Drag and Drop"
  description="Reorder, reparent, and place selected layers in Varve without losing hierarchy or spacing."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <main class="layers-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Layers & Drag and Drop
      </nav>

      <header class="page-hero">
        <StatusPill status="available" />
        <h1>Move ideas without losing the structure.</h1>
        <p>
          Reorder siblings, reparent into frames, and place a multi-selection on the canvas while
          Varve keeps the hierarchy, spacing, and document state together.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="feature-section" aria-labelledby="layers-navigation-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Selection without surprises</p>
        <h2 id="layers-navigation-title">Choose what a layer click does to the canvas.</h2>
        <p>
          Selecting a layer should not steal the view. In Varve's Layers options, choose
          <strong>Select only</strong>, <strong>Reveal when needed</strong>,
          <strong>Center selection</strong>, or <strong>Fit selection</strong>. The first keeps
          pan, zoom, and rotation exactly where they are; the others move the camera only as much
          as their names promise.
        </p>
        <div class="feature-grid">
          <article>
            <h3>Select only</h3>
            <p>Keep your working view while the selection and Inspector update.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Reveal or center</h3>
            <p>Keep zoom and rotation, then pan only when needed or center the resolved layer.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Fit selection</h3>
            <p>Frame the selected content with a predictable padded view, including multi-selection.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p>
          Tree focus, range selection, and modifier selection stay independent from camera motion.
          Explicit <strong>Reveal on Canvas</strong>, <strong>Center Selection</strong>, and
          <strong>Zoom to Selection</strong> commands remain available from the Layers context menu.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section" aria-labelledby="layers-range-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Two gestures, two jobs</p>
        <h2 id="layers-range-title">Scrub a selection without touching the hierarchy.</h2>
        <p>
          Press in the body of a Layers row and move through the visible stack to preview a
          contiguous range. Release commits it once, even when the list is virtualized or you
          reverse direction. The dedicated grip is reserved for structural reorder and reparent,
          so selecting a run never quietly changes document order.
        </p>
        <div class="feature-grid">
          <article>
            <h3>Stable range</h3>
            <p>Shift-click, Shift+Arrow, and row scrub share the same anchor and extent behavior.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Live but reversible</h3>
            <p>Rows preview before release; Escape, blur, or a cancelled pointer leaves the committed selection alone.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Handle-only structure</h3>
            <p>Use the grip when you mean reorder or reparent. The row body remains a selection surface.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section" aria-labelledby="layers-marquee-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Canvas object selection</p>
        <h2 id="layers-marquee-title">Marquee objects without confusing pixels and layers.</h2>
        <p>
          Drag empty canvas space with the Select tool to preview eligible objects on the active
          Design Canvas or page. The rectangle stays in screen space under camera rotation, while
          the pixel Marquee tool remains a separate raster-coverage workflow.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="layer-demo" aria-label="Illustration of the Layers panel and canvas handoff">
        <div class="layer-demo__panel">
          <div class="layer-demo__heading"><span>Layers</span><span class="layer-demo__dots">•••</span></div>
          <div class="layer-demo__row layer-demo__row--selected"><span class="layer-demo__grip">⋮⋮</span><span class="layer-demo__chevron">⌄</span><strong>Hero group</strong></div>
          <div class="layer-demo__row layer-demo__row--child"><span class="layer-demo__indent"></span><span class="layer-demo__chevron">⌄</span><span>Headline</span></div>
          <div class="layer-demo__row layer-demo__row--child layer-demo__row--selected"><span class="layer-demo__indent"></span><span class="layer-demo__chevron">⌄</span><span>Illustration</span></div>
          <div class="layer-demo__row"><span class="layer-demo__grip">⋮⋮</span><span class="layer-demo__chevron">·</span><span>Background</span></div>
          <div class="layer-demo__drop-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="layer-demo__canvas">
          <span class="layer-demo__canvas-label">Canvas</span>
          <div class="layer-demo__art layer-demo__art--back"></div>
          <div class="layer-demo__art layer-demo__art--front"></div>
          <span class="layer-demo__cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section" aria-labelledby="layers-workflow-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">A predictable gesture</p>
        <h2 id="layers-workflow-title">The preview is the promise.</h2>
        <p>
          The Layers tree resolves the destination under your pointer, then uses that same target
          for the insertion indicator, auto-expand, announcement, and document commit. Rows stay
          virtualized for large files, while the live cursor keeps the target current as the panel
          scrolls.
        </p>
        <div class="feature-grid">
          <article>
            <h3>Reorder and reparent</h3>
            <p>Move above, below, or into a frame or group. Mask-source clipping keeps its special semantics.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Multi-select that stays together</h3>
            <p>Selected roots travel as one operation. Descendants are not moved twice, and relative canvas spacing is preserved.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>One undoable change</h3>
            <p>Preview work stays transient. A completed hierarchy move becomes one coherent document history step.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="handoff" aria-labelledby="handoff-title">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Layers to canvas</p>
          <h2 id="handoff-title">Place a selection without flattening it.</h2>
          <p>
            Drop existing layers onto the canvas and Varve translates the group through world space
            into the active canvas or page. The first layer anchors the placement; the rest keep
            their offsets, transforms, and internal hierarchy.
          </p>
        </div>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Destination</dt><dd>Active Design Canvas or Print Page</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Selection</dt><dd>Canonical roots, ordered by the document</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Boundary</dt><dd>Cross-page transfer stays an explicit command</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section" aria-labelledby="layers-access-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">When dragging is not the right input</p>
        <h2 id="layers-access-title">Keyboard-ready and honest about boundaries.</h2>
        <p>
          Tree navigation, selection, expand/collapse, and move commands remain available from the
          keyboard. Locked, cyclic, stale, or unavailable destinations are rejected instead of
          pretending that a drop succeeded. External files are imported only by their eligible
          canvas surface, and native desktop drops retain their platform-specific limits.
        </p>
      </section>

      <aside class="honesty" aria-labelledby="layers-honesty-title">
        <h2 id="layers-honesty-title">Designed for documents that have a shape.</h2>
        <p>
          Varve keeps hierarchy semantics in the Layers system and ordinary collection ordering in
          shared sortable controls. That means a frame drop can mean “into,” while a page tab still
          means “reorder.” Each surface keeps its own persistence and history boundary.
        </p>
        <a href="https://github.com/K-Arthur/varve/blob/main/docs/architecture/layers-navigation.md">Read the Layers navigation contract →</a>
      </aside>

      <div class="feature-cta">
        <h2>Keep the layer stack working for you.</h2>
        <a href={sitePath('/download')} class="btn-default">Download Varve</a>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .layers-page { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0 5rem; }
  .breadcrumb { font-size: .875rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .page-hero { max-width: 700px; margin-bottom: 3.5rem; }
  .page-hero h1 { margin: 1rem 0; font: 700 clamp(2.3rem, 6vw, 4rem)/1.05 var(--font-editorial); color: var(--text-primary); letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  .page-hero p, .feature-section > p, .handoff p, .honesty p { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  .eyebrow { color: var(--accent-primary); font-size: .75rem !important; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .layer-demo { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(230px, .8fr) 1.4fr; min-height: 330px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); background: var(--surface-card); box-shadow: var(--elevation-shadow-raised); margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  .layer-demo__panel { position: relative; padding: 1.25rem .85rem; border-right: 1px solid var(--border-default); background: var(--surface-card); }
  .layer-demo__heading { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; padding: .25rem .6rem 1rem; color: var(--text-primary); font-size: .8rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .layer-demo__dots { color: var(--text-tertiary); letter-spacing: .16em; }
  .layer-demo__row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .55rem; min-height: 2.1rem; padding: .25rem .6rem; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: .9rem; border-radius: var(--website-radius-control); }
  .layer-demo__row--selected { color: var(--text-primary); background: var(--surface-accent-soft); }
  .layer-demo__row--child { padding-left: 1.65rem; }
  .layer-demo__grip { color: var(--accent-primary); font-size: .7rem; letter-spacing: -.18em; }
  .layer-demo__chevron { width: .7rem; color: var(--text-tertiary); }
  .layer-demo__indent { width: .7rem; }
  .layer-demo__drop-line { position: absolute; top: 9.8rem; left: 1rem; right: .75rem; height: 2px; background: var(--accent-primary); box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent-primary) 16%, transparent); }
  .layer-demo__canvas { position: relative; overflow: hidden; background: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent-primary) 12%, transparent) 0 1px, transparent 1.5px) 0 0 / 22px 22px, var(--surface-sunken); }
  .layer-demo__canvas-label { position: absolute; top: 1.2rem; right: 1.4rem; color: var(--text-tertiary); font-size: .72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .1em; }
  .layer-demo__art { position: absolute; border: 1px solid var(--border-accent); border-radius: .4rem; transform: rotate(-7deg); }
  .layer-demo__art--back { width: 45%; height: 42%; left: 22%; top: 28%; background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--brand-sandstone) 28%, var(--surface-card)); }
  .layer-demo__art--front { width: 45%; height: 42%; left: 34%; top: 38%; background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent-primary) 30%, var(--surface-card)); }
  .layer-demo__cursor { position: absolute; left: 69%; top: 62%; width: 1rem; height: 1rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--text-primary); border-top: 2px solid var(--text-primary); transform: rotate(-45deg); }
  .feature-section { margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  .feature-section h2, .handoff h2, .honesty h2 { margin: .5rem 0 1rem; color: var(--text-primary); font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.3rem); }
  .feature-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .feature-grid article { padding: 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-surface); }
  .feature-grid h3 { margin: 0 0 .5rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .feature-grid p { margin: 0; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; }
  .handoff { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.2fr .8fr; gap: 2rem; padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); margin-bottom: 4rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-accent); border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); background: var(--surface-accent-soft); }
  .handoff dl { margin: 0; }
  .handoff dl div { padding: .85rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-default); }
  .handoff dl div:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .handoff dt { color: var(--text-tertiary); font-size: .72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .handoff dd { margin: .25rem 0 0; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.5; }
  .honesty { padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); margin-bottom: 3rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); background: var(--surface-card); }
  .honesty a { color: var(--text-link); font-weight: 600; }
  .feature-cta { padding: 3rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default); text-align: center; }
  .feature-cta h2 { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.75rem; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .layer-demo { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .layer-demo__panel { border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-default); } .layer-demo__canvas { min-height: 240px; } .feature-grid, .handoff { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
